From: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: nss: create the mesh dbg_infra directory per device

The per-SoC mesh debug entries (links, mpp_mode) went into one dbg_infra
directory at the top of ath11k's debugfs tree, so on a board with more
than one radio - IPQ5018 with QCN6122 or QCN9074 - the second device's
debugfs_create_dir() failed ("'dbg_infra' already exists in 'ath11k'")
and its entries were never created. Put the directory under the device's
own debugfs directory, which exists by the time NSS is set up.

Signed-off-by: Andrei-Alexandru Bleortu <me@andrei-z.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/debug_nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/debug_nss.c
@@ -910,7 +910,7 @@ void ath11k_debugfs_nss_soc_create(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 {
 	struct dentry *debugfs_dbg_infra;
 
-	debugfs_dbg_infra = debugfs_create_dir("dbg_infra", debugfs_ath11k);
+	debugfs_dbg_infra = debugfs_create_dir("dbg_infra", ab->debugfs_soc);
 
 	debugfs_create_file("links", 0200,
 			debugfs_dbg_infra, ab,
